  "body": "## Scope and result\n\nThis adds `research/frontier1094-fixed-route-packing-cap/`, a source-bound, standard-library verifier and proof note. **No new \u03ba.** The selected #1094 data route has child ranks only 0, 8, 16, 32 and 48. Keep that **fixed child inventory** and the selected local word. Then no whole-helper owner reassignment into those children reaches complex primitive saving `a \u2265 0.001682094870065`. The exact rational interval root bracket is `(0.001682094870064, 0.001682094870065)`. Under the retained balanced conversion, the planning cap is `\u03ba < 0.001679270178313`, at most 0.395178% above the selected conditional \u03ba. The selected \u03ba reaches at least 99.606% of this favorable cap.\n\nThis narrows Douglas Colkitt's #1240 rank-51 halving cap (`\u03ba < 0.001687202645326`) under an explicit fixed-child premise. It is not a new construction, owner map, selected frontier or exact seven-step grid result. Axis transfer across child boundaries, or a route redesign that creates rank-49 through rank-51 children, is outside it.\n\n## Task card and overlap\n\n- `selected-packing`, priority revision 3, chooser nonce `51f534e584664a07443b4736c814deea`, scope key `ab5d8f0f0d19bbab8625`, refined to the fixed selected route's residual mass relaxation.\n- Package base and source pins `1f7a934975e5eacaf83511c9ac870263bf095e05`. None of the pinned inputs changed on main up to `0b1cccf8`, onto which this branch is rebased. Selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- Predecessor #1240 supplies the rank-51 coverage/halving model. The merged PR1276 bounds within-group idle-axis repartitions (ranks up to 51). The merged PR1387 sharpens that domain and gives a semantic counterexample. Their numerical caps are tighter but do not cover whole-helper reassignment among unchanged child bins. The open PR1685 shows that at `a = 0.00169` at most 1,603 idle mass units may sit at ranks \u2264 48, and asks which residual groups are legal. This package answers that for the fixed route: all of them have rank \u2264 48. PR1252 (open) repartitions across child boundaries and is outside this scope. PR1343/#1617/#1407 enumerate or construct concrete owner moves.\n- `scripts/find_overlap.py --refresh` was run at 2026-10-14 05:50 EDT (446 open PRs, 418 discussions). It is not a novelty certificate.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Route ranks.** The selected source manifest pins `DATA-PHASES.json` (SHA-256 `c5916ff3\u2026`), and those bytes equal the selected replay archive member. The checker recomputes the GF(2) rank of every idle child's `orthogonal_axes` in all 112 recipes.\n- **Capacities are the route ranks (review fix).** All 288 `(owner replica, child)` windows in the selected T16 `PLAN.json` have capacity equal to that child's route rank at every port. The two rank-0 children have no window.\n- **Hosting is a prefix (review fix).** All 69,120 hosted helpers in the selected `OWNERS.json.gz` lie in their windows. The owner map is pinned by the selected manifest and by `SPEC.json`. In every one of the 32,256 groups, the offsets tile `[0,U_g)` with `U_g \u2264 C_g`, and the remainders `C_g\u2212U_g` reproduce the replay's idle profile `{1:2276, 3:377, 7:7, 48:4866}` exactly. This is the hosting proof's prefix and remainder rule, checked on the selected data.\n- **Mass split.** The replay, `SPEC.json` and `PLAN.json` are bound by hash. The checker splits the complete profile into the per-call local word `{1:2412,2:418,3:432,4:142,5:82,8:8}` and idle mass 237,024, and checks PR1012's identity `1,041,408 = 72\u00b714,336 + 64\u00b7144`.\n- **Bound.** For `0<a<1`, an idle child of rank `r \u2264 48` costs at least `r\u00b748^(-a)\u00b773^(a-1)`. So the normalized complex moment is at least `[144 \u03a3_r local_r (r/73)^(1-a) + 4938 (48/73)^(1-a)]/14336`. A code-disjoint rational interval engine (reduced-argument atanh, Taylor remainder bounds) certifies both root endpoint signs. It independently reproduces #1240's rank-51 bracket.\n- **Controls.** Five mutations must each fail at their intended check: rank/axes mismatch, a rank-49 route child, mass-preserving local-word drift applied consistently to plan and replay, a window capacity of 49, and an overlapping hosted offset.\n\n## Reproduce and limits\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/frontier1094-fixed-route-packing-cap/verify.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/frontier1094-fixed-route-packing-cap\n```\n\nBoth pass on macOS with Python 3.12, and the standalone verifier passes on 3.10 and 3.14 (about 4 s). `tests.test_research_onboarding` and `tests.test_research_replay_selection` pass on the rebased branch. Not run: a cold selected replay, Linux CI and independent human review.\n\nThe calculation assumes fixed data-route child boundaries, PR1012's coverage law, the existing hosting operation and the retained balanced transfer. It relaxes timing, physical capacity and indivisible-helper constraints. All inherited all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source, whole-call hosting, precision/tape, analytic and bit H1\u2013H5 obligations remain.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nCan a capacity-aware relaxation within this fixed route rule out the hypothetical all-rank-48 allocation? Can an exact redesigned data route create rank-49 through rank-51 children without an offsetting controller or supplier charge? The README gives first steps and blockers.\n\n## Credit and assistance\n\nDouglas Colkitt and Claude: #1240 packing ceiling. PR1012: coverage identity. Rohan Arun and Jeremy Kothe: selected #1094 word and the T16 owner-packing line. The selected review records further data-route, controller, supplier and composition predecessors.\n\nPrepared by Josie Elliston with substantial AI assistance. OpenAI Codex drafted the package offline (session 14 of a donated overnight run). Claude (Anthropic) reviewed it, added the source-bound capacity and offset checks, fixed a control that was being rejected for the wrong reason, refreshed overlap and published it. A separate read-only Codex review flagged both fixes. No independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
